{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Who misleads a blind man</b> — meaning: do not advise him according to your way in order to move his boundary." "<b>משגה</b> — two times in the Masorah: משגה עור / משגה ישרים בדרך רע. This one, whose root is משגה עור, misleads by advising to sin. That one, משגה ישרים בדרך רע, is one who is upright yet gives him counsel to pervert his ways. And it is juxtaposed to it."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:10:50.900433922Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}